23 0 obj
<< /A 369 0 R /Alt (Schematic illustration of epigenetic changes after intracerebral hemorrhage. Hematoma formation and red blood cell lysis produce hemoglobin/iron overload, reactive oxygen species, damage-associated molecular patterns, and inflammatory mediators. These signals affect astrocytes, microglia, neurons, and brain microvascular endothelial cells. The main regulatory mechanisms include DNA methylation, histone modifications, chromatin remodeling, non-coding RNA regulation, histone lactylation, and m6A-related regulation. These changes are linked to astrocyte reactivity, microglial inflammatory and repair programs, neuronal dysfunction, blood-brain barrier disruption, leukocyte infiltration, and secondary brain injury.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
